    "overview": "The Colchis slow worm (Anguis colchica) is a legless anguid lizard. Tarkhnishvili et al. 2026 treat it as a candidate species: it belongs to the widespread western Eurasian A. fragilis complex; Gvoždík et al. (2010) elevated the Caucasian form (A. f. colchica) to species rank. It is likely allopatric with A. graeca and A. fragilis; cytochrome b difference from those relatives is 6.5–8%. That does not confirm species rank in this atlas — it remains a candidate. It is often confused with the European glass lizard or with snakes. The checklist figure is from Nigoeti; barcodes are from Mtisdziri environs, Baniskhevi, and Lanchkhuti. It is harmless to people.",
