        "Snout–vent length in a large Turkish series was about 4.4–6.7 cm (mean near 5.9 cm); original measurements were slightly larger. The tail is often longer than the body; one male reached about 18.7 cm total length. Arribas and co-authors (2021) found the Charnali dryada form larger, with a longer head in adult males and more dorsal scales, than typical clarkorum. A full Georgian measurement series is not on this page.",
